--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,22 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## On-device article translation
+
+Use the **Read in** bar on news pages to choose a language and select **Translate**.
+The browser's built-in [Translator API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api)
+translates article headlines, summaries, captions, body text, and teasers locally.
+The first use of a language may download a language pack; download and translation
+progress appear in the bar. **Show original** cancels pending work and restores
+the English text. Switching languages always translates from the saved English
+original, avoiding compounded translation errors.
+
+This feature needs a supported desktop browser and a secure context (HTTPS or
+localhost). Browser, device, and language-pair support are checked at runtime.
+Unsupported browsers keep the English content and display an explanation. There
+is no cloud translation fallback, API key, or translation service dependency.
+Language selection is local to the current page and resets after navigation.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
